warning[identity_op]: `x + 0` is just `x`: `+` with this operand changes nothing
  --> tests/lint/identity_op/bad.jai:5:10
   |
 5 |     a := x + 0;
   |          ^^^^^
   |
help: write `x`
   |
 5 ~     a := x;
   |
   = note: `identity_op` is `warn` by default

warning[identity_op]: `1 * x` is just `x`: `*` with this operand changes nothing
  --> tests/lint/identity_op/bad.jai:6:10
   |
 6 |     b := 1 * x;
   |          ^^^^^
   |
help: write `x`
   |
 6 ~     b := x;
   |
   = note: `identity_op` is `warn` by default

warning[identity_op]: `x - 0` is just `x`: `-` with this operand changes nothing
  --> tests/lint/identity_op/bad.jai:7:10
   |
 7 |     c := x - 0;
   |          ^^^^^
   |
help: write `x`
   |
 7 ~     c := x;
   |
   = note: `identity_op` is `warn` by default

warning[identity_op]: `(x | 0)` is just `x`: `|` with this operand changes nothing
  --> tests/lint/identity_op/bad.jai:8:11
   |
 8 |     d := (x | 0) * 2;
   |           ^^^^^
   |
help: write `x`
   |
 8 ~     d := x * 2;
   |
   = note: `identity_op` is `warn` by default

